        "whose robots tend the gardens and refuse all thanks",
        "where the founders’ promise is carved over every door",
        "whose skyline was designed by a committee of poets and engineers",
        "where the streets are swept by the wind and the rain",
        "whose festival of lights lasts a whole month",
        "where old disagreements are settled over long dinners",
        "whose doors have no locks",
        "where the sea wall is also a beach that runs for miles",
        "whose museums hold everything the city has ever thrown away",
        "where the whole city stops at sunset to watch the sky",
        "whose clean energy comes from the tides",
        "where every street ends in a fountain or a garden",
        "whose people seem a little too happy to visitors",
        "where the last prison was turned into a university",
        "whose founding charter is just one page long"
